## Original Content
Venture-capital firms are bringing AI and dealmaking to accounting, property management and other unglamorous fields.

## Summary
Venture-capital firms in Silicon Valley are now targeting traditional, low-margin businesses such as accounting and property management. They are integrating artificial intelligence and dealmaking strategies to innovate in these unglamorous fields. This shift indicates a growing investment in non-tech industries for potential growth opportunities.

## Key Points
- Venture capitalists are focusing on industries with thin profit margins.
- AI technology is being applied to transform traditional fields like accounting and property management.
- Dealmaking strategies are central to the integration of technology in these sectors.
- Silicon Valley is expanding its investments beyond high-tech ventures to include stable, non-glamorous businesses.


